<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa money mkt shortage jumps 2.4 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.Africa money mkt shortage jumps 2.4 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market surged 2.424 billion rand to 10.275 billion rand on Monday from 7.851 billion rand on Saturday, the Reserve Bank said on Tuesday. </p>
<p>Three-month NCD rates were quoted steady at between 16.45 to 16.65 percent and the 90-day BA rate was also unchanged at between 15.80 to 16.05 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
